WEBVTT

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:15.760
Don't miss that brightly shining light!

00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:20.870
It's always there beside you.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:26.420
I'm sure the rest just depends on your perception.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.590
You don't have to search for it—just notice that it's there!

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:37.350
There's a tenderness that lies hidden behind the most common things:

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:43.230
a light that showers our days in color!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:49.230
Tiny Days: This world is constructed...

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:54.800
Tiny Days: ...by fragments of miracles!

00:00:54.800 --> 00:01:00.180
Things that seemed meaningless

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:05.730
were actually protecting us, loving us, more than we ever knew.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:10.960
Tiny Heart: Our feelings flow forth...

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.000
Tiny Heart: ...as we give thanks for everything we've been given.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.490
We'll never, ever forget...

00:01:21.490 --> 00:01:27.700
We'll cherish this feeling forevermore!

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.990
Can a Sty-ko Who Can't Fly be Called "Sty-ko"?

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.900
Gotta pee...

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:13.210
Ao, is this a proper serving of rice?

00:02:13.460 --> 00:02:15.500
Oh! I'd say so!

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:18.820
I see.

00:02:22.820 --> 00:02:26.220
Hey, Sty-ko, do you and Base plan on staying here?

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.140
What's with that look?

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:30.060
"Sty-ko"?

00:02:30.060 --> 00:02:33.250
Yup! Sty-ko. I've decided to call you "Sty-ko."

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:37.240
Well? You're staying?

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:38.190
Yes. What of it?

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:42.320
Oh. Pets aren't allowed in this complex...

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:49.000
Well, it's not like it costs anything to feed you,
so I guess I'm okay with it.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:51.690
Even if you did try to get rid of me, you couldn't.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:53.060
Why not?

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:57.050
My pride wouldn't allow me to go back
without having beaten Gourai!

00:02:57.420 --> 00:03:00.640
So long as you collect your data,
it doesn't matter who wins or loses, right?

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:04.260
Uh... Well, yes, that's true...

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.520
What are you doing?!

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.400
I'm sorry. I thought Ao might like another serving.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.000
Oh, really? Thanks!

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:16.480
You eat as though it's quite delicious,
so I thought you might have room for more.

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.650
I sure do!

00:03:17.990 --> 00:03:20.700
By the way, my uncle sends me this rice!

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:23.160
That's quite helpful, isn't it?

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:25.450
You're content to blather on with this pointless conversation

00:03:25.450 --> 00:03:28.330
while I'm standing here covered in rice, aren't you?!

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:30.000
Ah, sorry 'bout that.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.730
I'll clean you up.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:38.920
Freeze!

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.050
Oh, there's more here.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:43.180
Freeze!

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:45.720
Stylet?

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:47.970
What's going on with you?

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.390
I-I don't know!

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:54.020
My body won't... it won't move!

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:57.360
Must be some kinda trauma, huh?

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:58.320
Trauma?

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:04.160
What does "trauma" mean?

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.990
Put simply, trauma is an emotional wound.

00:04:07.990 --> 00:04:11.750
Stylet totally couldn't stand it when she lost to Gourai.

00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:16.770
That's why her heart and her mind are all, like, mixed up and stuff. This has hurt her!

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.380
That makes sense.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.320
Base, you're actually pretty smart, aren't you?

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.680
M-Me?

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:29.930
Me? <i>I'm</i> traumatized?

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:32.520
Traumatized!

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:38.420
And it's Gourai's fault!

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:39.690
No, no. No!

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:42.800
There's no way that's possible. No way at all!

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.200
Freeze!

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:49.040
I knew it!

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:50.420
She's stiff as a board, huh?

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:51.790
No, I'm not!

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.870
Well, I mean...

00:04:53.870 --> 00:04:55.290
Hey! Cut that out!

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.960
You willing to admit that it's trauma?

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.570
N-No, I'm not!

00:05:02.050 --> 00:05:03.130
Charger-kun!

00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:10.560
Huh?

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.310
I can't fly?

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:13.310
Could that also be...

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:15.040
...because of the trauma?

00:05:15.650 --> 00:05:16.730
It can't be!

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:21.250
I-It can't be!

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:22.690
So this is...

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:24.280
It's a grave problem.

00:05:24.280 --> 00:05:28.220
We all share the same general-purpose control personality program,

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:33.020
but are installed with combat programs customized to our individual bodies.

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:39.920
Stylet's systems are optimized for aerial battle,
but this trauma may have caused functional impairment.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:43.670
If I can't fly... I'm just a...

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:50.510
Let's get Stylet... over her trauma!

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.060
Let the strategy meeting begin!

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.480
Yay!

00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:55.770
F.A. Girl!

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:01.270
Just what are you planning?

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.750
Now, now. Nothing to worry about.

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:05.360
Okay, here goes!

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.950
Go, go!

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.450
Oh! You're doing pretty well, Sty-ko.

00:06:14.500 --> 00:06:17.120
Let's get a little closer!

00:06:26.030 --> 00:06:28.650
Whoa... Look how close you got!

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.640
Huh? But what should we do next?

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:35.180
Hmm...

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:36.640
Dunno!

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:39.040
You don't know?

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:45.190
Ah! Shock therapy is supposed to cure trauma, right?

00:06:45.190 --> 00:06:48.910
Yeah! We could give her some BAM! POW! kinda shock!

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.450
Gourai!

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:53.390
S-Stylet...

00:06:53.870 --> 00:06:56.220
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:56.660
Go!

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:57.560
Just you watch!

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:12.990
I shall...

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:14.530
show you the way!

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:22.190
She used the Session Call!

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:23.040
I-I just...

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:24.540
Sparking!

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.120
This place...

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:47.230
What does Gourai think she's doing?

00:07:47.230 --> 00:07:49.510
Beats me. But it looks interesting!

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:19.700
Stylet.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:56.010
Ao, do you think this was an adequate form of shock therapy?

00:08:56.200 --> 00:09:00.370
H-Huh? Did I give some unneeded advice?

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.290
Winner: Gourai.

00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:06.250
F.A. Girl!

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:07.520
Ah, jeez.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:10.780
Stylet's circuits shorted out, huh?

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:15.280
What if we've just made things worse?

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.220
Uh, what is it?

00:09:20.430 --> 00:09:22.810
This is damaged, isn't it?

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:25.160
That's why Stylet can't fly.

00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.350
Huh?

00:09:26.350 --> 00:09:29.150
It seems like it was struck by some downward force.

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:37.160
I'm sorry. That was me!

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.080
What... happened?

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:43.520
You don't remember?

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:49.270
I remember you saying something about a strategy to cure my trauma,

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:53.840
and I was on the Session Base getting closer and closer to Gourai...

00:09:53.840 --> 00:09:56.900
Huh? What happened after that?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.930
Stylet, please try to fly.

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:06.270
Huh? But...

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.650
You're all right now.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:10.330
I am?

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.320
Yes!

00:10:13.190 --> 00:10:14.440
Then I'll try.

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:18.360
But it's not like I believe you or anything!

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:19.320
Okay.

00:10:21.870 --> 00:10:23.240
I'm flying!

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:30.770
Thank goodness. Thank goodness!

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:33.260
Sty-ko, that's great, isn't it?

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:36.760
Well, it's only natural that with that part repaired-!

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:42.120
I've overcome that trauma to become even stronger!

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:44.310
I deserve praise! I'm powerful!

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:49.850
Gourai! I want you to battle me this instant!

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:03.140
Wh-Wh-What is this?!

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:04.640
Why did this happen?!

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.470
Stylet?

00:11:07.210 --> 00:11:08.460
Freeze!

00:11:10.960 --> 00:11:12.500
My, this is...

00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.630
quite interesting!

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:20.950
We're Gonna Clean!

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.330
I'm home!

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:28.770
Here. I brought you all something.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:32.040
Woo-hoo! So, what is this round thing? A macaron?

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.020
That's right. It's the fabled jumbo macaron.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:37.780
No. Of course not! That's a cleaning robot!

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:39.010
A cleaning robot?

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:43.800
The building manager just gave it to me because he says he never uses it.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.510
And, like, our apartment's messy, right?

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:47.910
Wouldn't it be best to simply clean?

00:11:47.910 --> 00:11:49.350
No, no, no!

00:11:49.350 --> 00:11:53.250
Doing so would rob this thing of it's reason for being, right?

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:55.250
And we can't do that, right?

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:58.260
We, all of us, were born for the sake of someone else.

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:01.080
For someone else...?

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:06.430
Yes! And now, in this moment,
this cleaning robot is here for <i>me!</i>

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:07.700
I see.

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:11.380
Ao's kinda got a way with words.

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:14.290
Gourai is completely buying into it.

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:21.300
Incidentally, the emotions you're feeling for me right now are called "admiration" and "respect."

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:25.840
This is admiration and... respect?

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:30.250
Is it all right to leave Gourai's emotional data to Ao?

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.310
Beats me.

00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:33.640
So, I'll leave the repairs to you guys, okay?

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:35.080
What? "Repairs"?

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.650
The truth is, this thing is broken.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:42.300
Hey, Cleaning Robot-chan! You in there?

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:45.850
She's right. It's not doin' a thing!

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:50.740
Well, I'm gonna go meet up with Bukiko.

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:52.520
Bang this thing out while I'm gone, okay?

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:53.350
Just a moment!

00:12:53.350 --> 00:12:57.360
This is a very old model, made even before we were born!

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:02.610
This cleaning robot may have been born so that it could be fixed by <i>me.</i>

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:06.950
Whoa, wait, stop! What are you saying? Did some weird switch get flipped?

00:13:06.950 --> 00:13:09.810
Looks like Ao's influenced her, huh?

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:13.310
I get it, Ao! We shall fix this!

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:17.130
She took off a long time ago.

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:20.000
What does Ao take us for?!

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.800
Isn't it just that... she trusts us?

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.260
She's a little girl who depends on us.

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:27.910
Could a human ever be that way towards a Frame Arms Girl?

00:13:28.300 --> 00:13:32.140
Ao seems to already have childlike, dependent qualities.

00:13:32.140 --> 00:13:36.960
When she showed me her family album, there were several photos of her clinging to her parents.

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:42.320
Oh, jeez. So that's why Ao sometimes rubs her cheek up against her pillow in the middle of the night.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:43.070
Heh!

00:13:43.070 --> 00:13:44.280
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:50.740
Like, she'll rub up against the pillow muttering stuff. I've seen it!

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:54.350
So then... she's fawning over her pillow?

00:13:55.250 --> 00:13:56.770
That's too funny!

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:03.090
Oh, that's right! She also has a soft spot for poems.

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.030
Poems?

00:14:04.420 --> 00:14:05.550
Poems...

00:14:06.050 --> 00:14:10.350
Ao has a notebook full of poems. I read it the other day.

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:11.720
Without permission?

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:12.520
Yup!

00:14:12.520 --> 00:14:14.600
I didn't expect you to just go, "Yup!"

00:14:14.600 --> 00:14:20.320
Does this poetry notebook have lace and a blue ribbon on the cover?

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:21.090
That's the one!

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:23.900
I've read that as well.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:24.590
Huh?

00:14:25.450 --> 00:14:30.910
I was looking for something that would serve as data for learning more about emotions...

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:33.790
That's when I found those poems and...

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.540
"Poems <i>and"?</i>

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:43.980
What seemed to be her practicing her own autograph.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.260
P-Practicing her own autograph?!

00:14:46.260 --> 00:14:48.400
H-How embarrassing!

00:14:48.620 --> 00:14:52.970
Girls <i>do</i> practice their signature if they dream of being idols, though.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:59.430
"Birds. Wind. Clouds. The stars...

00:14:59.430 --> 00:15:02.570
They are all me, and I am them.

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:05.570
Tomorrow to the south, the day after to the north.

00:15:05.570 --> 00:15:06.990
Toot toot, beep beep.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:08.570
Boom shakalaka boom.

00:15:08.570 --> 00:15:10.530
Life is a journey.

00:15:10.530 --> 00:15:12.760
Yes... Let's go on that trip together."

00:15:13.740 --> 00:15:15.330
Wh-What the heck is that?

00:15:15.330 --> 00:15:17.560
One of Ao's poems, No. 85.

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:19.580
Stop!

00:15:21.840 --> 00:15:24.210
Ao's poem? "Poem"?!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.630
And it's No. 85?

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:28.220
She's written that many?!

00:15:28.930 --> 00:15:31.340
There are a lot more than 85...

00:15:31.340 --> 00:15:34.720
No. 85 was about halfway through the <i>first</i> notebook.

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:37.850
That's way too many poems!

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:54.200
Ao would lose it if she heard what we've been talking about, huh?

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:57.040
She might even throw us out.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:01.330
Because, to Ao, those are private.

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:06.320
Well, she gave us a lot of good laughs, so I guess we should fix this for her.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:10.970
Whoa, it's moving!

00:16:11.890 --> 00:16:14.280
It wasn't broken at all, was it?

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.560
"Birds. Wind. Clouds. The stars...

00:16:17.560 --> 00:16:20.290
They are all me, and I am them."

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.040
That voice just now!

00:16:22.270 --> 00:16:23.150
"Poetry notebook-"

00:16:23.150 --> 00:16:23.900
"Autograph?!"

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:24.690
"Idol-"

00:16:24.690 --> 00:16:26.540
"How embarrassing!"

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:31.530
So, that thing recorded our conversation?

00:16:31.530 --> 00:16:32.450
"Too funny!"

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:33.570
"Ao. Rubs."

00:16:33.570 --> 00:16:34.280
"Muttering."

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:34.700
"Ao."

00:16:34.700 --> 00:16:35.740
"How embarrassing!"

00:16:35.740 --> 00:16:36.490
"Heh!"

00:16:36.490 --> 00:16:40.100
It didn't just record us: it's jumbling together everything we've said!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.210
"For real, Ao-"

00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:42.120
"Super funny."

00:16:42.120 --> 00:16:43.670
"Like, for a human, super embarrassing!"

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:45.080
Why's it making us sound like schoolgirls?!

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:48.760
Wow... It's learning at such incredible speed!

00:16:48.760 --> 00:16:50.340
This is no time for admiration!

00:16:50.670 --> 00:16:55.110
If we don't do something,
we really could get thrown out, huh?

00:16:55.110 --> 00:16:57.350
I don't think she'd do that, but...

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:59.680
we could get the Charger-kun Punishment.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.620
"Charger-kun Punishment"?

00:17:01.890 --> 00:17:09.230
She could forcibly insert and withdraw the charge cord... and do it over and over!

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:22.660
What is this feeling?

00:17:22.660 --> 00:17:26.670
It's not like it hurts, but the thought gives me chills!

00:17:27.250 --> 00:17:29.800
For real, Ao's poems give me the chills!

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:31.840
For real!

00:17:31.840 --> 00:17:33.760
Anyway, catch that thing!

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.300
Understood!

00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:35.090
Gotcha!

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:41.680
Let's turn this off!

00:17:41.680 --> 00:17:42.890
Too funny!

00:17:46.270 --> 00:17:49.230
It's like a rodeo!

00:17:51.150 --> 00:17:52.880
Base is great!

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.760
Let's keep it going and...!

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.200
Yay, I got it!

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.460
Hm. Not bad.

00:18:08.130 --> 00:18:08.560
I'm ho-

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:09.440
What?!

00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.460
What is all this?!

00:18:11.820 --> 00:18:13.340
What have you been doing?!

00:18:13.340 --> 00:18:14.440
What happened to cleaning?!

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.630
And what about the cleaning robot?!

00:18:16.630 --> 00:18:20.260
Um, Ao, the cleaning robot is...

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.040
It wasn't broken after all.

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:24.950
But I broke it!

00:18:24.950 --> 00:18:26.460
What?

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:29.460
So, I'll battle Gourai.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:34.360
Ah, so she can collect the money from her "part-time job."

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.230
Yup!

00:18:35.230 --> 00:18:38.700
And she can use that to fix the cleaning robot, right?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:39.610
That's right!

00:18:39.610 --> 00:18:41.220
Well, okay then.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:44.200
Gourai!

00:18:44.200 --> 00:18:45.060
Baselard!

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:47.420
Frame Arms Girl Session...

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:48.230
Go!

00:19:02.350 --> 00:19:05.540
Full of excitement! Ba-baam!

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.810
I'm going to give you a slight fever of the heart!

00:19:15.820 --> 00:19:16.610
Gourai?

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:19.130
Just so we're clear, I'm pretty strong!

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.380
I won't be beaten!

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:21.840
Here I come!

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:26.330
Huh? This is just like...

00:19:26.330 --> 00:19:31.980
That's right: Baselard and I both specialize in aerial combat, which makes things tough for Gourai.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:35.020
All weapons systems... activate!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:40.720
Full Burst Mode!

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:45.410
What?! Base is trying to finish her off all at once!

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.290
Woo-hoo!

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:50.900
Gourai!

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:52.770
Huh?

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:58.860
Whaa? I'm shooting 'em all, but I can't hit her!

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:00.360
Chaff!

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:04.410
I see! It's because of all the dust that came out of that cleaning robot earlier.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:07.810
It's being dispersed in the air,
reducing Base's firing accuracy!

00:20:07.810 --> 00:20:10.790
Will that affect Gourai too?

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:13.080
No. Gourai uses actual bullets.

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.290
All right!

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.090
Gourai! Give her one, big blast!

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:16.880
Understood!

00:20:29.270 --> 00:20:30.730
Winner: Gourai.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:34.480
Jeez, I lost.

00:20:35.060 --> 00:20:38.400
Still, it was fun! Let's do that again, Gourai!

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:39.440
Sure.

00:20:39.820 --> 00:20:41.170
All right!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.280
This'll get me my pay!

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:45.120
And I can fix the cleaning robot too.

00:20:46.370 --> 00:20:47.720
I'm home!

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:50.750
Ao? What is that?

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:53.730
Uh, I'm not too sure myself.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.630
I ran into the building manager downstairs,

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:59.740
and when I told him I was getting the cleaning robot repaired, he handed me this.

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:01.420
That's a vacuum cleaner, right?

00:21:01.420 --> 00:21:03.260
But it really looks like...

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:04.720
a weapon!

00:21:04.720 --> 00:21:06.140
She's getting worked up, huh?

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:08.800
Good for you, Ao.

00:21:10.500 --> 00:21:14.100
They'll soon show up at your door,

00:21:14.100 --> 00:21:19.500
for my special someone, parts of hearts!

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:29.780
Counting the days I can't see you,

00:21:30.970 --> 00:21:37.230
I want to hear your voice so badly I feel like crying!

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:40.720
I'm new to this world,

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:44.190
so I lack the language to describe it.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:46.460
To knockoffs, say...

00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:49.910
"No!" Take care to avoid them.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:53.430
I want to be be dedicated!

00:21:56.820 --> 00:22:02.130
I want to build it all from nothing!

00:22:02.130 --> 00:22:05.360
We laugh and we fight,

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.970
creating our unique specs!

00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:14.890
By mixing love and hate,

00:22:14.890 --> 00:22:23.000
I want to create more of these funny, carefree days, the parts of Girl!

00:22:40.460 --> 00:22:43.760
Why do we make sounds when our chargers get plugged in?

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.280
Beats me!

00:22:45.280 --> 00:22:48.020
Next time, on Frame Arms Girl... All together now:

00:22:48.020 --> 00:22:48.320
Here Come the Materia Sisters
Let's Go to School

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:49.340
Session!

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:53.200
I just acted like I didn't care - but let's push in this recharging cord!

00:22:53.200 --> 00:22:55.020
Let's Go to School
Here Come the Materia Sisters
